1. The finding and its rule

  ADV-R-13 [Major] of `measure/runs/model_guide/adversarial-f6c29b0.json`.
  The routes `t/one#c` and `t-one#c` fold to one `RUN_SLUG`, so they shared
  one lock file and one output folder.

  The orchestrator decided on 2026-11-18: the lock file name appends the
  first 12 hex characters of the SHA-256 of the full route string to the
  slug, so each route has its own lock. The output folder name changes too
  when the test needs it, with the same suffix. Nothing else changes.

2. Change

  `harness/model-guide/review-run.sh` computes `ROUTE_TAG` as the first 12
  hex characters of the SHA-256 of the full route string. The lock file is
  `<private>/.locks/review-<set>-<slug>-<tag>-<date>.lock`, and the output
  folder is
  `<private>/outputs/<set>/<date>-<slug>-<tag>-p<pass>`. The record name
  keeps the plain slug.

  The output folder change is needed. Without it, the second route writes
  its staging file over the staging file of the first route. The first route
  then exits 1 on its `mv`. The orchestrator allowed this change with the
  same suffix.

  The script header names the new rule. No test file changed.

